# ── .state/.gitignore ──
# Track structure (start.md manifests), ignore accumulation.
# State is instance-specific — only the skeleton travels with the framework.

# Ignore everything
*

# Keep directory tree
!*/

# Keep manifests and this gitignore
!start.md
!.gitignore

# ── tests/ is run output, not structure ──
# `!start.md` above is UNANCHORED: it re-includes start.md at ANY depth. A mileqa
# run sandboxes a whole copy of the codex tree under tests/mileqa/<run>/sb/, and
# that copy carries ~30 start.md files of its own — every one of them was being
# un-ignored, so `git add .state` would have committed a duplicate codex.
# Exclude the output directories; keep the two real manifests.
tests/*/
!tests/audits/
